            {
                "entry_id": "e33c3420-a288-3407-9727-d7dab08211f3",
                "word": "naturalité",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "fr",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "ad409db2-3c39-40ca-8fc4-c154dd8f462c",
                        "entry_id": "e33c3420-a288-3407-9727-d7dab08211f3",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "naturalités"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "6858023e-c776-32f2-b47a-659e7c8f1cc9",
                        "entry_id": "e33c3420-a288-3407-9727-d7dab08211f3",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Caractère de ce qui est à l’état de nature, qui n’a pas été conçu ou travaillé par la main humaine."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "cca57fa1-c6d8-444f-bfc1-1c411109a541",
                                "sense_id": "6858023e-c776-32f2-b47a-659e7c8f1cc9",
                                "text": "Dans cette sphère domine la contradiction de la liberté et de la servitude car d’un côté l’âme est encore attachée à sa substantialité elle est conditionnée par sa naturalité pendant que de l’autre côté elle commence à s’affranchir de sa substance de sa naturalité et s’élève ainsi à une sphère intermédiaire entre sa vie naturelle immédiate et la conscience objective et libre."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "fe3891c9-2c32-36c7-9312-0fd8ccb3ecc3",
                        "entry_id": "e33c3420-a288-3407-9727-d7dab08211f3",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Caractère sauvage d’un paysage ou d’un milieu naturel."
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "c2396015-9e65-4f53-b7da-d70ee10843f4",
                                "sense_id": "fe3891c9-2c32-36c7-9312-0fd8ccb3ecc3",
                                "text": "Le degré d’altération des forêts se traduit évidemment par une baisse générale de naturalité parmi les populations animales, dont certaines ne sont plus viables (Grand Tétras, Gélinotte, gros coléoptères xylophages entre autres)."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "89ea815e-8514-48f7-afa6-0b050731a691",
                                "sense_id": "fe3891c9-2c32-36c7-9312-0fd8ccb3ecc3",
                                "text": "Nous pouvons suivre Ratcliffe (1977) qui associe la naturalité à l’ancienneté de l’écosystème et à l’absence de signes de perturbation due à l’homme."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "a057399d-b069-4897-bf34-e30194f220cc",
                                "sense_id": "fe3891c9-2c32-36c7-9312-0fd8ccb3ecc3",
                                "text": "Changer notre regard sur les forêts et œuvrer en faveur de leur naturalité évitera leur dégradation au niveau planétaire et des conséquences dramatiques dans tous les domaines, économique et politique, écologique, social et culturel."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "4fc5da0d-54b9-3e45-a7ac-2489057ee09e",
                        "entry_id": "e33c3420-a288-3407-9727-d7dab08211f3",
                        "glosses": [
                            "Qualité de celui ou de celle qui devient ressortissant d’une nation, qui bénéficie d’une naturalisation ; nationalité."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "dated"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "ea9d0f88-c181-4d31-8edf-e689655da13c",
                                "sense_id": "4fc5da0d-54b9-3e45-a7ac-2489057ee09e",
                                "text": "Le jeune comte ayant pris part à l’insurrection polonaise, est venu chercher un asile en France, où la juste célébrité de son talent lui a valu des lettres de petite naturalité. »"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "168eac80-cf24-4607-b88f-550001da19e9",
                                "sense_id": "4fc5da0d-54b9-3e45-a7ac-2489057ee09e",
                                "text": "Tu seras madame Brunner de Marville, dit le père à sa fille, car j’obtiendrai pour ton mari la permission de joindre ce nom au sien, et plus tard il aura des lettres de naturalité. Si je deviens pair de France, il me succédera !"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "36773df5-c498-47d6-8fb2-236dc2bca3b0",
                                "sense_id": "4fc5da0d-54b9-3e45-a7ac-2489057ee09e",
                                "text": "Toutefois cette faveur n’était accordée qu’aux étrangers catholiques ; car la catholicité était une question préalable, que l’on examinait avant d’accorder la naturalité."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "b6aaae4d-aef0-4913-8385-a25d1b785920",
                                "sense_id": "4fc5da0d-54b9-3e45-a7ac-2489057ee09e",
                                "text": "Nous avons découvert une autre copie, très voisine de la précédente, dans un manuscrit de la Bibliothèque nationale rassemblant notamment cinq pièces relatives à la naturalité du Cardinal : […]."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "704757a7-dfab-4e0a-9ab1-93c1f2cf84bc",
                        "source_entry_id": "e33c3420-a288-3407-9727-d7dab08211f3",
                        "target_lang_word": "Wildnis",
                        "target_lang_code": "de",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "Wildnis",
                                "target_lang_code": "de",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "32c637ac-a05f-318e-b5c1-91e979e055c9",
                                        "entry_id": "44f18113-1b13-34a2-ab90-76d8b16957ec",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "ein vom Menschen unbeeinflusstes Gebiet (auf der Erde)"
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c48e580d-2024-4421-9d6a-a92a4326df46",
                                                "sense_id": "32c637ac-a05f-318e-b5c1-91e979e055c9",
                                                "text": "Sie kamen über die Elbe und siedelten bis hinauf zur Eider, rodeten die Wildnis und betrieben Ackerbau und Viehzucht."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "40520220-b290-45a8-85db-e5c7eb7142eb",
                                                "sense_id": "32c637ac-a05f-318e-b5c1-91e979e055c9",
                                                "text": "Empfanget mich, ihr stillen Wildnisse der Fremde und gebet mir die längst ersehnte Ruhe!"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "5504b6bc-91f9-470a-ba85-e54004e8b72d",
                                                "sense_id": "32c637ac-a05f-318e-b5c1-91e979e055c9",
                                                "text": "„Im Januar 1880 zerschneiden erste Straßen die Wildnis, stehen ein Verwaltungsgebäude, Häuser und Maultierställe, gebaut aus Fertigteilen einer Londoner Firma.“"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "beba571a-30da-4e7d-896e-522973252ee3",
                                                "sense_id": "32c637ac-a05f-318e-b5c1-91e979e055c9",
                                                "text": "„Unser 500-Kilometer-Trip durch die Wildnis war vorüber.“"
                                            }
                                        ],
                                        "sense_index_json": "\"1\""
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "translation_id": "37ba9f31-f8df-4e40-8a57-488995805f1b",
                        "source_entry_id": "e33c3420-a288-3407-9727-d7dab08211f3",
                        "target_lang_word": "wilderness",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "wilderness",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "eddb0183-08a9-32b4-9afb-a789755f9965",
                                        "entry_id": "d3637ed0-7165-30f9-a7a0-9488765351a2",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Uncultivated and unsettled land in its natural state inhabited by wild animals and with vegetation growing wild; (countable) a tract of such land; a waste or wild."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "113a7c9f-7e84-40b7-b9bf-a12771adb416",
                                                "sense_id": "eddb0183-08a9-32b4-9afb-a789755f9965",
                                                "text": "For ſtill he traueild through wide waſtfull ground, / That nought but deſert wilderneſſe ſhewed all around."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d3887498-462e-4130-8f0a-efe020cf927e",
                                                "sense_id": "eddb0183-08a9-32b4-9afb-a789755f9965",
                                                "text": "O my poore kingdome! ſicke with ciuill blowes: / VVhen that my care could not withhold thy riots, / VVhat wilt thou do when riot is thy care? / O thou wilt be a wilderneſſe againe, / Peopled with woolues, thy old inhabitants."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "02039016-9b40-4c61-9018-15a30bfab76b",
                                                "sense_id": "eddb0183-08a9-32b4-9afb-a789755f9965",
                                                "text": "Behold, as wilde aſſes in the deſart, goe they foorth to their worke, riſing betimes for a pray: the wildernes yeeldeth food for them; and for their children."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4ea4cd6f-efb8-40a3-a020-6116dd02d631",
                                                "sense_id": "eddb0183-08a9-32b4-9afb-a789755f9965",
                                                "text": "Strange it is, that he reporteth of the miraculous workes of ſome of them, that they may ſeeme (as he ſaith) incarnate Deuils: […] ſome dwell amongſt men, ſome by themſelues apart, and ſome in Wilderneſſe: […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3dab850b-bfb7-4c98-87ca-6323ae1219c2",
                                                "sense_id": "eddb0183-08a9-32b4-9afb-a789755f9965",
                                                "text": "Thus they went on talking of what they had ſeen by the way; and ſo made that way eaſie, which would otherwiſe, no doubt, have been tedious to them: for now they went through a Wilderneſs."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "09dd870c-d2ea-403b-a1ee-28176e2010d2",
                                                "sense_id": "eddb0183-08a9-32b4-9afb-a789755f9965",
                                                "text": "Oh for a lodge in ſome vaſt wilderneſs, / Some boundleſs contiguity of ſhade, / Where rumour of oppreſſion and deceit, / Of unſucceſsful or ſucceſsful war / Might never reach me more."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0cbab00e-beba-452f-b39f-885bb7647da2",
                                                "sense_id": "eddb0183-08a9-32b4-9afb-a789755f9965",
                                                "text": "Miss Bennet, there seemed to be a prettyish kind of a little wilderness on one side of your lawn. I should be glad to take a turn in it, if you will favour me with your company."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "bc0492a7-bdc8-4687-98fd-7dae8b6f26fc",
                                                "sense_id": "eddb0183-08a9-32b4-9afb-a789755f9965",
                                                "text": "Here they ascended, and anon appeared to descend in the same direction, finding only boundless wildernesses, and varied combinations of tangled woodland scenery."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b811df8a-9d09-424a-8e3a-7ccec1a15c57",
                                                "sense_id": "eddb0183-08a9-32b4-9afb-a789755f9965",
                                                "text": "[…] I can conceive nothing more likely to set the youthful blood into a flow, than a wild wood life of the kind, and the range of a magnificent wilderness, abounding with game, and fruitful of adventure."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "3ccf9e34-6612-45eb-b2fb-e95f0281b988",
                                                "sense_id": "eddb0183-08a9-32b4-9afb-a789755f9965",
                                                "text": "Down from the bastion'd walls we dropt by night, / And flying reach'd the frontier: then we crost / To a livelier land; and so by town and thorpe, / And tilth, and blowing bosks of wilderness, / We gain'd the mother-city thick with towers, / And in the imperial palace found the king."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "1328db81-680c-37fb-989f-fa408e357bd5",
                                        "entry_id": "d3637ed0-7165-30f9-a7a0-9488765351a2",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A place other than land (for example, the air or sea) that is uncared for, and therefore devoted to disorder or wildness."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "broadly",
                                            "countable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "114a1a89-d117-4cf4-9bb6-901a8596a7c1",
                                                "sense_id": "1328db81-680c-37fb-989f-fa408e357bd5",
                                                "text": "For now I ſtand as one vpon a rocke, / Inuirond with a wildernes of ſea, / VVho markes the vvaxing tide, grovv vvaue by vvaue, / Expecting euer vvhen ſome enuious ſurge, / VVill in his briniſh bovvels ſvvallow him."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "eb4e565b-af66-4804-9118-68fb9b8f38ee",
                                                "sense_id": "1328db81-680c-37fb-989f-fa408e357bd5",
                                                "text": "[W]hat / Is this blue wilderness of interminable / Air, where ye roll along, as I have seen / The leaves along the limpid streams of Eden?"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "bece47ea-789a-3079-b6bc-d3dbef43f461",
                                        "entry_id": "d3637ed0-7165-30f9-a7a0-9488765351a2",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "An ornamental part of a garden or park cultivated with trees and often a maze to evoke a natural wilderness."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "broadly",
                                            "countable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "53367428-160e-430a-bd61-0f3e023f232c",
                                                "sense_id": "bece47ea-789a-3079-b6bc-d3dbef43f461",
                                                "text": "And now with nerves new-brac'd and ſpirits chear'd / We tread the wilderneſs, whoſe well-roll'd walks / With curvature of ſlow and eaſy ſweep, / Deception innocent—give ample ſpace / To narrow bounds."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "571176d6-3c2f-376d-83c1-9d816bc3bc6f",
                                        "entry_id": "d3637ed0-7165-30f9-a7a0-9488765351a2",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Unrefinedness; wildness."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "broadly",
                                            "obsolete",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "de6d096e-21c1-4907-8524-0e334de32a97",
                                                "sense_id": "571176d6-3c2f-376d-83c1-9d816bc3bc6f",
                                                "text": "What ſhould I thinke, / Heauen ſhield my Mother plaid my Father faire: / For ſuch a warped ſlip of wilderneſſe / Nere iſſu'd from his blood.",
                                                "translation": "What should I think? / Heaven forbid, my mother must have been unfaithful to my father, / For such a warped descendant of wildness / Never issued from his blood.",
                                                "english": "What should I think? / Heaven forbid, my mother must have been unfaithful to my father, / For such a warped descendant of wildness / Never issued from his blood."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "227af7cb-3de5-4217-a698-9fd8d0e46da1",
                                                "sense_id": "571176d6-3c2f-376d-83c1-9d816bc3bc6f",
                                                "text": "Theſe paths & Bowers doubt not but our joynt hands / Will keep from Wilderneſs with eaſe, as wide / As we need walk, till younger hands ere long / Aſſiſt us: […]"
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "eb67b58a-b1f4-39c8-84ed-52851701adc0",
                                        "entry_id": "d3637ed0-7165-30f9-a7a0-9488765351a2",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Chiefly followed by of: a bewildering flock or throng; a large, often jumbled, collection of things."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "figuratively",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "4a8366cf-b7c7-47af-88f5-7c497b31910a",
                                                "sense_id": "eb67b58a-b1f4-39c8-84ed-52851701adc0",
                                                "text": "Tuball. One of them ſhewed me a ring that hee had of your daughter for a Monkey. / Shy[lock]. Out vpon her: thou tortur'ſt me Tuball, it was my Turkies, I had it of Leah when I was a Batchellor: I would not haue giuen it for a wilderneſſe of Monkies."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "97cb8012-f286-473b-ade7-05097d1ce9a7",
                                                "sense_id": "eb67b58a-b1f4-39c8-84ed-52851701adc0",
                                                "text": "[T]he virgins thou haſt rob'd of all their wiſhes, / blaſted their blowing hopes, turn'd their ſongs, / their mirthful Marriage-ſongs to Funerals, / the Land thou haſt left a wilderneſſe of wretches."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "c83f8734-8ad8-47cd-9f93-551e52c51aba",
                                                "sense_id": "eb67b58a-b1f4-39c8-84ed-52851701adc0",
                                                "text": "Thir glittering Tents he paſsd, and now is come / Into the bliſsful field, through Groves of Myrrhe, / And flouring Odours, Caſſia, Nard, and Balme; / A Wilderneſs of ſweets; […]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "71ddea00-de3f-4dfb-86c1-09ca7b5221d8",
                                                "sense_id": "eb67b58a-b1f4-39c8-84ed-52851701adc0",
                                                "text": "And as she treats all things, and ne'er retreats / From any thing, this Epic will contain / A wilderness of the most rare conceits, / Which you might elsewhere hope to find in vain."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "d407dc8a-7014-4003-9171-57dcd2c3f82f",
                                                "sense_id": "eb67b58a-b1f4-39c8-84ed-52851701adc0",
                                                "text": "Tortured by these thoughts he carried monotony with him, through the rushing landscape, and hurried headlong, not through a rich and varied country, but a wilderness of blighted plans and gnawing jealousies."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "be445eec-bfa8-4d14-9446-e9f1829d0f90",
                                                "sense_id": "eb67b58a-b1f4-39c8-84ed-52851701adc0",
                                                "text": "He had but glanced away at the piles of city roofs and chimneys among which the smoke was rolling heavily, and at the wilderness of masts on the river, and the wilderness of steeples on the shore, indistinctly mixed together in the stormy haze, when she was again as quiet as if she had been plying her needle in his mother's room."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "70415ee1-a19c-398c-899d-67f2117000d3",
                                        "entry_id": "d3637ed0-7165-30f9-a7a0-9488765351a2",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "A place or situation that is bewildering and in which one may get lost."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "figuratively",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "ebda63d5-4c17-4959-9b52-e2dc8b98a830",
                                                "sense_id": "70415ee1-a19c-398c-899d-67f2117000d3",
                                                "text": "As I walk'd through the wilderneſs of this world, I lighted on a certain place, where was a Denn; And I laid me down in that place to ſleep: And as I ſlept I dreamed a Dream."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "6d02e4e9-172b-4e5d-a935-33101ec5ddc9",
                                                "sense_id": "70415ee1-a19c-398c-899d-67f2117000d3",
                                                "text": "If solitude succeed to grief, / Release from pain is slight relief; / The vacant bosom's wilderness / Might thank the pang that made it less."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2d8af7be-63a7-42d0-a4a2-bd9a901d20ca",
                                                "sense_id": "70415ee1-a19c-398c-899d-67f2117000d3",
                                                "text": "Where to go? Still somewhere, anywhere! still going on; but where! She thought of the only other time she had been lost in the wide wilderness of London—though not lost as now—and went that way. To the home of Walter's uncle."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "19431430-41dc-479c-9dc9-4e649728b79b",
                                                "sense_id": "70415ee1-a19c-398c-899d-67f2117000d3",
                                                "text": "The dim, dusty room, with the busts staring down from the tall book-cases, the cosy chairs, the globes, and, best of all, the wilderness of books, in which she could wander where she liked, made the library a region of bliss to her."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "ac854006-9d18-3625-8da3-a6539ed75781",
                                        "entry_id": "d3637ed0-7165-30f9-a7a0-9488765351a2",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "Preceded by in the: a situation of disfavour or lack of recognition; (specifically, politics) of a politician, political party, etc.: a situation of being out of office."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "figuratively",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "b3c5c1f0-d7cc-46ef-a167-acd9cff9d518",
                                                "sense_id": "ac854006-9d18-3625-8da3-a6539ed75781",
                                                "text": "After the firm establishment of the Irish Free State, [Winston] Churchill would continue to hold office until the depression. Then, he found himself in the political wilderness. But, unlike [David] Lloyd George, he would not find himself tripping to Berchtesgaden to prostrate himself before Adolf Hitler in admiration. Perhaps he had learned something from Michael Collins—never bend the knee to the tyrant."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    }
                                ]
                            }
